## Verdict

- r145's DRAFT ceiling for C3 (≤ ~9.8% of DKG base) came in **RAN-confirmed at 9.85%** —
  the top of the band. C3's range family is a real 38.38% of its leaf — the same class
  as C2a's 38.23% (marginally above it), on a leaf ~2× the size.
- The single biggest *priced* reducible surface across both paths remains the C3 range
  family; the honest caveat is that it is the same soundness-loaded class as C2a's, so
  "cut it" still requires a chip-level/aggregate redesign (r115 C6 class), not a NOP.
- Browser P3 asymmetry stands undisturbed: <3.8% (r132) vs ~38% here — the per-coeff
  range family is a DKG-side problem, not a browser-side one.

